Package: respkit
Type: Package
Title: Reusable Tools for Respiratory Belt Signal Processing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Norman", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "norman@radlab.zone")
Description: A dataset-agnostic toolkit for processing respiratory
    signals recorded from strain-gauge belts, nasal thermistors, or
    similar continuous respiration transducers. Provides a self-describing
    recording container with honest sampling-rate bookkeeping, exact
    multistage decimation, artefact cleaning, two peak/trough detection
    algorithms, a per-breath morphology table (duration, inspiratory and
    expiratory time, duty cycle, amplitude, respiratory volume per time),
    window/epoch aggregation with variability metrics, and signal quality
    assessment. Task-specific paradigm logic is deliberately excluded so
    the same code can be reused across studies.
